<ContentLayout title="About Kryos" description="About the Kryos computing ecosystem and its development." heading="About Kryos." lead="Kryos is an independent computing ecosystem centered on Kryos OS, with Veckt as its browser workstream.">
  <section class="section shell article-content">
    <h2>One ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="content-copy"><strong>Kryos OS</strong> is the foundation of the project: an operating system being built from scratch in Rust. <strong>Veckt</strong> is the browser workstream being developed alongside it. The aim is to build connected software with a coherent approach to security, privacy, reliability and user choice.</p>
    <h2>What matters to the project</h2>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Correctness</h3><p>Build behavior that can be specified, reviewed and tested.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Security</h3><p>Make authority, privilege and trust boundaries explicit.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Reliability</h3><p>Protect user data and communicate limitations clearly.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Performance</h3><p>Measure resource use and latency rather than relying on assumptions.</p></article>
    </div>
    <h2>Current availability</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Kryos is still in development. Neither Kryos OS nor Veckt has a public release. There are no public installers or user documentation yet.</p>
    <h2>Project stewardship</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Kryos is an independently developed computing ecosystem. Official project repositories and release channels will be listed here as their public identities are finalized.</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>